  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2022, relating to authorizing the\nassessor of the county of Nassau to accept from the Mineola Union Free School\nDistrict an application for exemption from real property taxes, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 8940-A and A.9981-A, in relation to making\ntechnical amendments therefor",
    "basePrintNo": "S2232",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2232-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.8940-A & A.9981-A)",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2232\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2022, relating to authorizing\nthe assessor of the county of Nassau to accept from the Mineola Union\nFree School District an application for exemption from real property\ntaxes, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8940-A and A.9981-A,\nin relation to making technical amendments therefor\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.466.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by making technical\nchanges to ensure the preservation of local approval for the tax\nexemption.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 14 of 2022, the Executive and Legislature\nreached this agreement to make a technical change to ensure that the\nNassau County Legislature has the ability to approve the exemption at\nlocal option.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 466 of the Laws of 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date as a chapter of the laws of\n2022 authorizing the assessor of the county of Nassau to accept from the\nMineola Union Free School District an application for exemption from\nreal property taxes, as proposed in legislative bill number S. 8940-A,\ntakes effect.\n",
